 ## Sharing a VM
 
 The full app and an embedding app open the same VM in the default folder ([finding the VM](#finding-the-vm)), never at once: the VM folder's lock refuses the second. The run mode reports `vm-already-open`, and the full app says that Omarchy is open in another app, such as Omarchy Installer. Either can boot a VM the other made. The `try-omarchy` package only upgrades, so an older kit never downgrades the guest. A launcher refuses a VM whose `vm.json` names a storage layout it does not know (`storage-layout-unknown`).
+
+### Focused clipboard routing (private POC patch)
+
+The native clipboard bridge reads and writes the Mac clipboard only while its exact QEMU process is frontmost and its captured kernel process identity is still alive. Unknown focus fails closed. It needs no additional Accessibility grant. Focus gain synchronizes the current Mac clipboard once; a background guest's clipboard and sync messages are ignored. A quarter-second poll reconciles focus, and each clipboard side effect checks focus again on the bridge's serial state queue. Echo markers reset at observed focus loss/gain. If a guest message first observes focus gain, the current host selection wins that transition.
+
+The global Mac clipboard still transfers content intentionally when the user switches guests. The change prevents background broadcast and background writes; it does not create private host clipboards. The client configuration and run protocol remain at version 1. Deterministic two-route tests cover shared pasteboard isolation, rapid activation, focus loss during reads and immediately before side effects. Real two-guest focus behaviour remains to be validated on Apple Silicon.
+
+The headless clipboard helper keeps the main run loop running and performs its blocking guest-channel read on a worker queue. Every foreground lookup runs synchronously on the main thread, including lookups requested by the serial routing queue. The real POC found that an otherwise idle main loop could leave worker-only AppKit foreground polling stuck on an old app; main-thread lookups tracked the same focus cycle correctly. Tests exercise the actual focus adapter from both threads, matching and mismatching foreground PIDs, unavailable focus and stale process identities, alongside reader completion and error propagation. The correction does not change protocol 1 or any bridge/configuration fields.
